  "decision": "Stop typed-subscription direction. Measured irrelevant bodies 0.721ms/frame plus conservatively charged six-empty-listener full-broadcast calibration 0.155ms/frame = estimated 0.876ms/frame before replacement routing cost. No evidence of >1ms/frame net saving; no production implementation.",
  "limitations": [
    "0.876ms is a conservative empirical candidate-cost estimate, not a mathematical bound or measured whole-frame gain. Empty signal calibration uses same engine headless and may differ from rendered workload.",
    "Listener bodies include Callable.call overhead and timer effects; no-op calibration charges entire six-listener broadcast, including empty callback invocation, so some call overhead is double-counted conservatively. No correction was sold as a performance improvement.",
    "Raw emit residual 1.042ms/frame still includes wrapper entry/exit, lookup and extra Callable invocation. It is not pure engine dispatch and cannot be added as removable cost without accounting for probes.",
    "Separate empty-listener calibration estimates full wrapping perturbation; 1.362ms/frame measured bookkeeping is only part of it. Whole-frame 31.825ms is instrumented and must not be compared to prior 27.54ms as a regression or saving.",
    "Three diagnostic listeners are excluded from production-removable work. Main battlefield listener remains necessary; no damage text, muzzle or effect work counted as removable.",
    "No nested selected emits or other nested listener calls occurred; arithmetic reconciliation verifies emit inclusive = listener exclusive + measured bookkeeping + residual for each kind.",
    "Initial probe connection attempt was invalid because static bound callbacks collided; it is discarded entirely. Unique per-listener forwarding objects were then used for the only accepted full sample."
